          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Genesis AI unveils GENE-26.5, its first full-stack robotics model, with dexterous hand demo",
            "articleSection": "Discovery & Research",
            "abstract": "Genesis AI, a Khosla Ventures-backed startup that raised a $105 million seed round to develop foundational AI for robotics, has publicly unveiled its first model, GENE-26.5, alongside a demo showing robotic hands performing complex dexterous tasks. The startup is positioning itself as a full-stack robotics AI company, meaning it handles both the perception and control layers of robotic intelligence. The demo represents one of the most advanced publicly shown examples of AI-driven robotic dexterity from a seed-stage company.",
            "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/06/khosla-backed-robotics-startup-genesis-ai-has-gone-full-stack-demo-shows/",
            "publisher": {
